\title{Continuations and Sharding}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    Splitting a long execution into segments that can be proved independently and in parallel. The mechanism that makes zkVM proving a distributed job rather than a single machine's problem.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{Segmenting a trace: what state must be carried across a boundary, and how it is committed.}
        \li{The consistency argument between shards, especially for [memory](dhsorens-003U).}
        \li{Aggregating shard proofs into one, and the recursion tree's shape.}
        \li{How SP1 and RISC Zero each do it, and what their differences imply.}
        \li{The soundness surface this adds — a shard boundary is a place to forget a constraint.}
    }
}
